<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       ELIJAH, THE HUNDREDTH — the warden at the top of the Tower of Gods.

       She climbed it. She won. Godhood settled on her exactly as it settles
       on the player who kills her, and then the tower kept her: the order
       that ran this place promoted her into it and afterwards died out, which
       is the same order whose verdict the Archangel's Wrath still carries
       with nobody left to enforce it. She has held the post ever since, for a
       purpose that died with the people who assigned it, and she cannot tell
       the player what the tower is for because she was never told either.

       Named for the prophet taken up alive in a whirlwind — Hebrew Eliyahu,
       "my God is Yahweh": an oath of service, worn by someone nobody came
       back to relieve.

       SHE IS DATA. Everything except four runtime details (white aura, the
       ascendant hediff, the VPE grant, the wing overlay) lives in this file,
       so she can be rebalanced without touching C#. See ElijahWarden.cs.
       ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

  <!-- Her aura. AuraSystem overrides the rank palette with the pawn's
       favoriteColor, so one ColorDef is the entire "her aura is white"
       feature. Shipped here rather than borrowed from Ideology's LightGrey
       because that def is DLC-gated and is not actually white. -->
  <ColorDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_AngelicWhite</defName>
    <label>angelic white</label>
    <color>(1, 1, 1)</color>
  </ColorDef>

  <!--
    THE ASCENDANT BODY. Half of "she never goes down" is here and half is on
    her PawnKindDef, because vanilla splits the two causes:

      pain          → PawnKindDef.ignoresPainShock (below), pure data
      everything else → Pawn_HealthTracker.ShouldBeDowned, which this hediff
                        gates through a narrowly-scoped Harmony prefix

    PSYCHIC COMA gets its own treatment in the comp: its stage uses
    setMax 0.1 on Consciousness, and a setMax cannot be beaten by any offset
    a hediff could add — so it is removed rather than resisted. That covers
    VPE's neural-heat coma too, which uses the same vanilla def.

    blocksMentalBreaks is the same vanilla field Godhood uses. She is holding
    a post she cannot leave; she is long past being able to panic about it.

    SHE HAS THE GODHOOD BODY, and that is the floor's lesson. Everything the
    trait will shortly do FOR the player is done first TO them: she cannot die
    of damage, of blood loss, of a failed organ or of shock, and the only thing
    that ends her is a destroyed brain. A player who has fought that knows
    exactly what the letter is handing them.

    ElijahWarden attaches IsekaiDungeons_GodhoodBody at generation, so the rule
    is literally the same comp a colonist carries rather than a copy of it.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Ascendant</defName>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <label>ascendant</label>
    <labelNoun>ascension</labelNoun>
    <description>This one went up the tower and did not come back down. Whatever she is now does not tire, does not faint, and does not lose consciousness for any reason short of death — the body has been held upright for longer than anyone has been counting, and it has forgotten how to stop.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(255, 223, 128)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <scenarioCanAdd>false</scenarioCanAdd>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <initialSeverity>1.0</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1.0</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <blocksMentalBreaks>true</blocksMentalBreaks>
        <statOffsets>
          <!-- Belt and braces with ignoresPainShock: this also keeps her
               fighting normally at high pain rather than merely upright. -->
          <PainShockThreshold>10.0</PainShockThreshold>
          <PsychicSensitivity>4.0</PsychicSensitivity>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
    <comps>
      <li Class="IsekaiDungeons.HediffCompProperties_Ascendant"/>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    HER BODY IS THE ART. Elijah_body_{south,north,east}.png is a complete
    character - head, hair, wings and halo in one sprite - so it is installed
    as a BodyTypeDef graphic rather than layered on as an overlay. That is the
    vanilla path: bodyNakedGraphicPath is a Graphic_Multi prefix, and the three
    facings are exactly the files that were drawn.

    HER SIZE IS NOT SET HERE. bodyGraphicScale looks like the size lever and is
    not one: the entire game reads it in two places, PawnRenderNodeWorker
    .OffsetFor (behind drawData.scaleOffsetByBodySize) and
    PawnRenderNodeWorker_AttachmentBody, and both scale the OFFSET of
    attachment nodes. Neither touches the body graphic. Two attempts at sizing
    her this way (1.35, then 2.0) changed nothing whatsoever.

    What resizes her is the base mod's render-scale registry
    (WorldBossSizePatch.RegisterRenderScale). For a humanlike the part that
    matters is its postfix on HumanlikeMeshPoolUtility, since a humanlike's
    mesh never reads the graphic's drawSize. She opts into it with
    ElijahWarden.RenderScale, which is where her size actually lives. Left at 1
    here because she wears no apparel and her head node is a transparent
    placeholder, so there is no attachment offset worth scaling.

    THE WINGS ARE WHY THE NUMBER IS LARGE. Measured on the art, her body is
    only 0.54 of the texture width and the outstretched wings take the rest, so
    any scale applied to the whole texture buys a bit over half as much body as
    it looks like it should.

    The art must stay SQUARE and consistent across facings. Graphic_Multi hands
    every facing one drawSize, so three different aspects (they shipped at
    1.152, 1.085 and 0.868) get squeezed onto the square quad by three
    different amounts - which is what made her look stretched vertically. All
    three are now 1024x1024, a power of two, so they also get the full mip
    chain instead of a clamped one.
  -->
  <BodyTypeDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahBody</defName>
    <bodyNakedGraphicPath>Pawns/Elijah_body</bodyNakedGraphicPath>
    <bodyDessicatedGraphicPath>Pawns/Elijah_body</bodyDessicatedGraphicPath>
    <bodyGraphicScale>(1.0, 1.0)</bodyGraphicScale>
  </BodyTypeDef>

  <!--
    A DELIBERATELY EMPTY HEAD. The art already contains her face and hair, so
    the vanilla head node must draw nothing rather than stack a second head on
    top of the sprite. An 8x8 fully transparent Graphic_Multi is the least
    invasive way to say that: no render-tree surgery, no Harmony, and every
    system that expects a pawn to HAVE a head type still finds one.

    Her hair and beard are set to Bald/NoBeard in the spec below for the same
    reason.
  -->
  <HeadTypeDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahHead</defName>
    <graphicPath>Pawns/Elijah_blankhead</graphicPath>
    <gender>Female</gender>
  </HeadTypeDef>

  <!--
    Her kind. ignoresPainShock is the load-bearing line — Pawn_HealthTracker
    .InPainShock early-outs on it, so no amount of damage puts her into shock.

    BasePlayerPawnKind generates NOTHING: no weaponTags, no apparelTags, and
    isFighter false. That is fine and deliberate, because the character spec
    below dresses and arms her explicitly — but it is also why the spec MUST
    list gear. A spec with clearExistingApparel and no apparel list would
    strip her naked, and with no weapon she would fist-fight the endgame.

    combatPower 1200 is documentation, not mechanism: she is only ever spawned
    by name. (It does not read as Nation to the roster band guard either —
    MobRankUtility.CalculateBaseRankFromThreatScore tops out at S — which
    costs nothing here precisely because she is never rolled from a roster.)
  -->
  <PawnKindDef ParentName="BasePlayerPawnKind">
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahKind</defName>
    <label>the hundredth</label>
    <race>Human</race>
    <combatPower>1200</combatPower>
    <isFighter>true</isFighter>
    <!-- Required of every humanlike kind or RimWorld logs a config error at
         startup ("initial resistance range is undefined"). 0 is honest: she
         cannot be captured or recruited, so the number is never consulted. -->
    <initialResistanceRange>0~0</initialResistanceRange>
    <ignoresPainShock>true</ignoresPainShock>
    <!-- 0 as a guard. She can never be downed
         (Pawn_HealthTracker_ShouldBeDowned_AscendantPatch), so vanilla's
         death-on-downed roll should never reach her. If something ever downs
         her anyway, that roll would take her brain, and for a preventsDeath
         pawn it re-enters itself and crashed ("Tried to restore null body
         part"); see GodhoodBrainDeathPatch.cs. -->
    <overrideDeathOnDownedChance>0</overrideDeathOnDownedChance>
    <destroyGearOnDrop>false</destroyGearOnDrop>
    <defaultFactionDef>IsekaiDungeons_MirrorFaction</defaultFactionDef>
  </PawnKindDef>

  <!--
    THE CHARACTER. Read by IsekaiCharacterForge.Generate through
    ElijahWarden.CharacterDefName.

    STATS: strength, vitality and wisdom, in that order, and almost nothing
    else. She is a front-line caster who does not die: she hits like the thing
    that killed whatever used to guard this floor, she absorbs punishment
    because she cannot be put down, and her wisdom is what carries the fire.
    Dexterity, intelligence and charisma are left low on purpose — she is not
    quick, not clever, and has not spoken to anyone in a very long time.

    Level is left UNSET so the forge derives it from the allocation exactly the
    way an organic pawn's is; the rank trait then follows the level, and the
    rank/level mismatch this system exists to prevent cannot happen here.
    The allocation below lands her at Nation.

    faction is the mirror faction — "the tower's hand". She IS the tower's
    hand, so it needs no second faction of its own, and it is already hidden,
    permanently hostile, and generation-neutral (baseliner).
  -->
  <IsekaiLeveling.CharacterForge.IsekaiCharacterDef>
    <defName>IsekaiDungeons_Elijah</defName>
    <spec>
      <pawnKind>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahKind</pawnKind>
      <faction>IsekaiDungeons_MirrorFaction</faction>

      <firstName>Elijah</firstName>
      <nickName>Elijah</nickName>
      <lastName>the Hundredth</lastName>
      <gender>Female</gender>
      <!-- Biologically stopped on the day she reached the top. The
           chronological figure is how long ago that was. -->
      <biologicalAgeYears>24</biologicalAgeYears>
      <chronologicalAgeYears>1000</chronologicalAgeYears>

      <!-- Her art IS her appearance. -->
      <bodyType>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahBody</bodyType>
      <headType>IsekaiDungeons_ElijahHead</headType>
      <hairDef>Bald</hairDef>
      <beardDef>NoBeard</beardDef>
      <!-- PURE WHITE, not the marble Godhood tint: the body graphic is
           multiplied by skin colour, so anything darker would dim the artwork.
           White leaves the sprite exactly as it was drawn. -->
      <skinColorOverride>(1, 1, 1)</skinColorOverride>

      <clearExistingTraits>true</clearExistingTraits>
      <traits>
        <!-- The halo and the gold name come free with this: GodhoodHalo draws
             on the trait, and TraitColorPatch paints on the trait. The
             GodhoodBody reconciler only ever touches COLONISTS, so the body
             hediff (and its preventsDeath) is NOT from here: ElijahWarden
             attaches it deliberately. -->
        <li><def>Isekai_Godhood</def><degree>0</degree></li>
        <li><def>Isekai_IronWill</def><degree>0</degree></li>
      </traits>

      <!-- STR / VIT / WIS. -->
      <strength>420</strength>
      <vitality>400</vitality>
      <wisdom>380</wisdom>
      <dexterity>90</dexterity>
      <intelligence>70</intelligence>
      <charisma>40</charisma>

      <constellation>Mage</constellation>

      <skills>
        <li><def>Melee</def><level>20</level><passion>2</passion></li>
        <li><def>Shooting</def><level>12</level><passion>0</passion></li>
        <li><def>Intellectual</def><level>16</level><passion>1</passion></li>
        <li><def>Medicine</def><level>10</level><passion>0</passion></li>
        <li><def>Social</def><level>4</level><passion>0</passion></li>
      </skills>

      <!-- A WEAPON IS MANDATORY, APPAREL IS FORBIDDEN. Her kind rolls neither
           (BasePlayerPawnKind has no weapon or apparel tags), so without this
           she would fist-fight the endgame. Apparel is deliberately absent and
           cleared: worn clothing renders OVER the body graphic, and the body
           graphic is a finished character - a duster drawn across those wings
           would ruin the one thing this floor is for. Her defence is 400
           vitality and an inability to be knocked down, not a flak vest.

           The longsword is Core so a bare install still arms her;
           ElijahWarden.UpgradeWeapon swaps in the archangel blade when Isekai
           Creatures is present. -->
      <weapon>
        <def>MeleeWeapon_LongSword</def>
        <stuff>Plasteel</stuff>
        <quality>Legendary</quality>
      </weapon>
      <clearExistingApparel>true</clearExistingApparel>
    </spec>
  </IsekaiLeveling.CharacterForge.IsekaiCharacterDef>

</Defs>
